WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.093
(Anna laughs)
(audience claps)

2
00:00:01.093 --> 00:00:04.830
So you're working at Zagat, you're fact checking,

3
00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:06.300
you're signature dishing.

4
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.133
(Anna laughs)

5
00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:09.870
You have your illustrious acting career

6
00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:11.300
in the rear-view mirror.

7
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.500
Where are you at and what brings you back?

8
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.850
See, I would say my illustrious acting career

9
00:00:17.077 --> 00:00:19.480
was ahead of me at that point,

10
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:22.920
because what was behind me was not my choice, right?

11
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:26.570
But in front of me was living in New York,

12
00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:29.170
going to see Broadway shows all the time,

13
00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:32.850
standing in the TKTS line and getting to see Broadway.

14
00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:36.890
And that was when it really started,

15
00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:39.720
kind of the Jiminy Cricket on my shoulder saying,

16
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.200
you should try this again, yeah.

17
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:43.770
But was that the only voice

18
00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:45.520
that told you to go back to acting?

19
00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:47.713
There was like a...

20
00:00:47.713 --> 00:00:51.709
for about a month, I was getting these signs from just-

21
00:00:51.709 --> 00:00:52.910
The universe?

22
00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:55.260
Jung would've called it the synchronicity.

23
00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:58.513
And yeah, I met Roberta Flack at a nail salon.

24
00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:00.330
Just wacky.

25
00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:02.960
And I met her and she asked what I was doing.

26
00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:04.720
I said, "Oh, I'm done with show business."

27
00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:06.480
And she looked at me like I had seven heads

28
00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:09.013
and she was like, why would you not?

29
00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:12.910
So it just stuck with me.

30
00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:16.560
And then the straw that broke the camel's back

31
00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.830
was I was on a lunch break crying,

32
00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:20.720
'cause you cry on a lunch break when you're sad

33
00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.794
and in your 20s sometimes.

34
00:01:22.794 --> 00:01:24.572
I love you.
(Anna laughs)

35
00:01:24.572 --> 00:01:25.500
Go on.

36
00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:28.820
I'm walking towards Madison Avenue to get a burger,

37
00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:32.640
and there was a psychic who was always handing out

38
00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.060
her pamphlets on 53rd and Madison.

39
00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:38.420
And she was, you know, "Oh, I have a question for you."

40
00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:39.253
And I'm like, "Yeah, yeah."

41
00:01:39.253 --> 00:01:41.750
That's what you say, that's what you say to advertise.

42
00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:45.340
And she followed me and...

43
00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:47.870
she poked on my shoulder.

44
00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:49.570
I turn around,

45
00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:50.490
you know, a mess.

46
00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:51.970
And she's like, "I have a question."

47
00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:52.960
I'm like, "What?"

48
00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:54.350
She says, "Are you the girl from 'My Girl'?"

49
00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:57.680
I'm like, "Ugh, yes." (laughs)

50
00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.966
You know, great psychic, and so then-

51
00:01:59.966 --> 00:02:03.410
(audience laughs)
(Drew laughs)

52
00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:05.230
But then she says...

53
00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:10.230
Then she said, "You're not done, you still wanna do this."

54
00:02:10.863 --> 00:02:12.270
Then I was like, (groans)

55
00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:14.590
I mean, it was...

56
00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:19.590
It was $40 for a 10 minute palm reading on my lunch break.

57
00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:22.067
On an editorial assistant's salary,

58
00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:25.090
$40 on a lunch break really meant a lot to me.

59
00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:27.453
But I did, I got my palm read.

60
00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:34.750
But really the message was, you need to try this again.

61
00:02:36.157 --> 00:02:38.840
You aren't done, you're wondering if you need to try.

62
00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:41.607
And so that stuck with me, yeah.

63
00:02:41.607 --> 00:02:44.368
(audience claps)

64
00:02:44.368 --> 00:02:46.280
And you saw this psychic.

65
00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:48.394
There's a pack of tarot cards here.

66
00:02:48.394 --> 00:02:49.227
(Anna laughs)

67
00:02:49.227 --> 00:02:50.230
How did this come about?

68
00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:51.883
You read tarot cards?
I do.

69
00:02:51.883 --> 00:02:53.500
This is years later now.

70
00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:55.651
This is 20 years later.
Do they connect?

71
00:02:55.651 --> 00:02:57.234
This, you know...

72
00:02:59.229 --> 00:03:00.190
How do I start?

73
00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:02.930
I first saw my first deck of tarot,

74
00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:04.310
I think my dad brought it into the house

75
00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:07.803
'cause he was exploring our Roma heritage.

76
00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:11.350
That's our heritage which is always very connected

77
00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:13.020
with psychics and tarot,

78
00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:14.930
and dancing bears and whatever.

79
00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:16.810
And we have that in our heritage too.

80
00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:21.410
And then I didn't look at it for a long, long time.

81
00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:25.763
And then I was in a play in 2018

82
00:03:25.763 --> 00:03:29.160
at Second Stage with an actor named Stephen Park

83
00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.430
who reads tarot.

84
00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:34.150
And so we got used to everyday just pulling a card.

85
00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:36.320
And once that show was over

86
00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:39.080
and he was no longer in my life everyday with his cards-

87
00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:39.960
You missed it.
I missed it.

88
00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.902 line:15%
And I learned and I learned.

89
00:03:41.902 --> 00:03:45.069 line:15%
(upbeat bright music)

